       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as no more than about 850\u20131000 mg per dose. A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Pharmacy will probably flag it."
      }
